<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!-- Debug builds only: tells Android Auto that Jacket has something to listen to, so the lists
         ListenService offers ("Continue listening", "Recent books") can be tried in a car or in
         the Desktop Head Unit. A build that isn't from Google Play only shows there with Android
         Auto's "Unknown sources" developer setting switched on.

         Release builds leave it out on purpose. Declaring it puts every Google Play release
         through the Android Auto review, and Jacket isn't ready for that yet (see
         docs/roadmap.md). When it is, the entry below and res/xml/automotive_app_desc.xml move to
         the main manifest.

         One thing that review asks for is known to be missing, and lint is told so here rather
         than left to fail every debug build: an activity that takes "play ... on Jacket" from the
         phone's assistant (android.media.action.MEDIA_PLAY_FROM_SEARCH). In the car, a book asked
         for by name already reaches ListenService through its media session. -->
    <application tools:ignore="MissingIntentFilterForMediaSearch">
        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.car.application"
            android:resource="@xml/automotive_app_desc" />
    </application>
</manifest>
